'''''Australina pusilla''''', the '''small shade nettle''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Urticaceae]], native to eastern Australia, and New Zealand.<ref name="POWO_163245-3" >{{cite POWO |id=163245-3 |title=''Australina pusilla'' (Poir.) Gaudich. |access-date=16 October 2022 }}</ref><ref name="FoAv3p93" >{{cite book |last1=George |first1=Alexander S. |date=1989 |title=Flora of Australia: Volume 3; Hamamelidales to Casuarinales |url=https://www.dcceew.gov.au/sites/default/files/env/pages/a08d125d-a6d0-47c4-85e9-9b7ac5d4931a/files/flora-australia-03-hamamelidales-casuarinales.pdf |location=Canberra |publisher=Australian Government Publishing Service |page=93 }}</ref> A highly variable perennial herb reaching {{cvt|50|cm|in}}, it is often found growing alongside shady streams.<ref name="FoAv3p93" />

==Subtaxa==
The following subspecies are accepted:<ref name="POWO_163245-3" />
*''Australina pusilla'' subsp. ''muelleri'' {{small|(Wedd.) Friis & Wilmot-Dear}} – Queensland, New South Wales, Victoria, Tasmania
*''Australina pusilla'' subsp. ''pusilla'' – New South Wales, Victoria, Tasmania, North Island, South Island

